Can you help me set up my voicemail message?

110
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:13,310
I just got the service and I'm not really sure what I'm supposed to say.

111
00:05:13,710 --> 00:05:14,090
Sure.

112
00:05:14,610 --> 00:05:20,410
You just basically got to let the caller know who they called and ask them for their contact information so you can call them back.

113
00:05:20,790 --> 00:05:21,050
Okay.

114
00:05:21,230 --> 00:05:23,790
So I can say, this is Abby's voicemail.

115
00:05:24,330 --> 00:05:25,230
I will call you later.

116
00:05:25,410 --> 00:05:26,750
So leave me your name and number.

117
00:05:27,190 --> 00:05:30,230
That's more or less the idea, but try something that sounds more friendly.

118
00:05:30,890 --> 00:05:31,330
Okay.

119
00:05:31,390 --> 00:05:32,550
So how about this?

120
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:35,340
This is Abby and I'm really happy you called.

121
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:38,440
I promise I will give you a ring as soon as I can.

122
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:40,480
So please leave me your name and number.

123
00:05:40,860 --> 00:05:41,660
Talk to you soon.

124
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:44,180
A little too friendly, Abby.

125
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:45,220
Just say this.

126
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:46,900
Hi, you've reached Abby.

127
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:52,080
I'm unable to answer your call right now, but if you leave me your name and phone number, I will get back to you as soon as possible.

128
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:52,680
Thanks.

129
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:53,920
That's perfect.

130
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:56,740
Can you say that again and record it for me?

131
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:04,860
All right, here we are in Fluency Builder and the first phrase we've got is, how about this?

132
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:09,280
So we're saying, we've got an example for you.

133
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:10,220
How about this?

134
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:11,000
That's right.

135
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:11,940
Then the example.

136
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:16,040
So we've talked about how about many times already.

137
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:23,000
So for example, how about we go to the movies or how not to say how about your weekend because that's completely wrong.

138
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:28,000
In this occasion, we're talking about how about this and this is like setting it up for an example.

139
00:06:28,350 --> 00:06:28,670
That's right.

140
00:06:28,790 --> 00:06:36,290
So for another example, we could say, so Marco, I'm trying to figure out how to say hello when I answer the phone because I don't like the way I say it now.

141
00:06:36,830 --> 00:06:37,790
I can say, how about this?

142
00:06:38,510 --> 00:06:38,870
Hello?

143
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:40,840
Is that good?

144
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:41,840
No?

145
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:42,170
That's all right.

146
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:43,840
That's right.

147
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:44,840
Hello.

148
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:45,840
That's too strong.

149
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:46,310
Yeah, that's good.

150
00:06:47,150 --> 00:06:47,490
All right.

151
00:06:47,650 --> 00:06:50,670
So basically I'm setting up an example.

152
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:52,720
I'm saying, okay, keep listening.

153
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:53,610
I will give you an example.

154
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:54,380
Yeah.

155
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,960
Just imagine that you're trying on different clothes and someone is giving you their opinion.

156
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:02,580
So maybe you try on a black shirt and you say, how about this one?

157
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:04,040
Eh, boring.

158
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:06,920
And then you try on a green one and you say, now how about this?

159
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:07,920
Better.

160
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:08,920
Right.

161
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:14,040
So then you're giving them other options and examples and this is why we say, how about this?

162
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:16,800
And then we give the example like Abby did.

163
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:19,140
And you're also asking for a response.

164
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,020
You're asking for an opinion.

165
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:28,520
And so what Abby's saying is, I promise I will give you a ring as soon as I can.

166
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:37,740
Now this phrase, give you a ring is very British English, but it's also something you should know if you want to be in America because you'll hear it in TV and stuff.

167
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:39,280
That's right.

168
00:07:39,280 --> 00:07:41,560
It's actually a colloquial term for saying, I will call you.

169
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:42,680
I will call you.

170
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:44,940
I will call you back or I will give you a call.

171
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:46,580
So the telephone rings.

172
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:49,150
That's the verb that goes with the phone, right?

173
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:50,960
Ring ring.

174
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:54,650
So I will give you a ring means I will call you just like you just said, Marco.

175
00:07:55,180 --> 00:07:55,350
That's right.

176
00:07:56,180 --> 00:07:57,250
So remember this phrase.

177
00:07:57,640 --> 00:08:01,730
It's actually, it may seem a little bit confusing, but remember it has to do with calling someone.

178
00:08:02,030 --> 00:08:04,330
I will give you a ring is I will call you.

179
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:06,770
Or if you say, hey, give me a ring later on this afternoon.

180
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:09,360
It's call me later this afternoon.

181
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:10,130
All right.

182
00:08:10,440 --> 00:08:15,610
And then moving towards the end of the dialogue, Abby says, hi, you have reached Abby.

183
00:08:16,130 --> 00:08:16,410
Okay.

184
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:20,680
This is weird because she is Abby, but she's saying you have reached Abby, right?

185
00:08:20,830 --> 00:08:22,470
You're speaking about yourself in the third person.

186
00:08:22,670 --> 00:08:22,870
That's right.

187
00:08:23,090 --> 00:08:23,750
So this is a message.

188
00:08:24,410 --> 00:08:25,810
So you're telling people what to do.

189
00:08:25,950 --> 00:08:26,690
Like I said, they're instructions.

190
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:32,240
And so this is basically the first thing you say, you have reached Catherine.

191
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:36,280
That means the number you dialed is Catherine's phone number, right?

192
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:38,390
So you reached, that means that you've contacted.

193
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:39,440
Right.

194
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:39,870
Exactly.

195
00:08:40,680 --> 00:08:58,000
So as you said, it's important if you ever call a bank or in, or any type of company, it will say you have reached a Wells Fargo bank or something, and it'll give you, it'll tell you what number you called because maybe you put in your finger wrong and you just called the wrong number.

196
00:08:58,220 --> 00:08:58,460
That's right.

197
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:00,360
Or you could use the word reached in a different way.

198
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:04,000
For example, yesterday I was very angry at Marco because I couldn't reach him by phone.

199
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:07,160
I called and called and called and couldn't reach him.

200
00:09:07,160 --> 00:09:09,320
And I realized then his phone is broken.

201
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:09,530
That's right.

202
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:15,270
So actually this verb to reach someone also has to do with, with, in general with calling.

203
00:09:15,530 --> 00:09:18,420
I was trying to reach you all afternoon, but I couldn't get a hold of you.

204
00:09:18,430 --> 00:09:19,040
That's right.

205
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:20,840
And I was so frustrated.

206
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:29,960
Well, actually, if I had voicemail, I would continue by saying, I am unable to answer your call right now because maybe my phone is off.

207
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:31,240
Maybe I am busy.

208
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:35,160
So we say, I am unable to answer your call right now.

209
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:36,160
All right.

210
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:37,160
Now this seems really long.

211
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:38,160
Okay.

212
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:44,720
It's a little bit strange, but this is basically the standard for how to record a message.

213
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:46,550
I'm unable to answer your call right now.

214
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:48,090
So you answer the phone, right?

215
00:09:48,350 --> 00:09:49,790
Or you answer a phone call.

216
00:09:50,370 --> 00:09:55,350
But in this case, I'm unable to, that means I can't talk to you for whatever reason.

217
00:09:55,570 --> 00:09:56,410
I'm out of the house.

218
00:09:56,630 --> 00:09:57,030
I'm busy.

219
00:09:57,670 --> 00:10:00,250
So I'm unable to answer your call right now.

220
00:10:00,390 --> 00:10:02,890
Just remember that that means I can't talk to you right now.

221
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,280
I can't be on the phone.

222
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:10,100
And actually this word unable sounds a lot more polite and a lot more formal than saying I can't.

223
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:10,800
That's right.

224
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:15,400
And that's why we use it on messages like this because it is so polite and so nice.

225
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:15,600
That's right.

226
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:16,520
All right.

